  "slug": "bilayer-graphene-energy-spectrum-3476",
  "summary": "Four preprints extend electronic-structure modeling to external fields, fictitious-temperature DFT, electron force fields and exciton-phonon workflows.",
  "synthesis": "The four preprints extend electronic-structure descriptions beyond standard ground-state treatments, through learned models, reduced models, functional parameterization and workflow codes. MLEH-LR adds long-range interactions and external fields to a machine-learning electronic Hamiltonian, applied to boron nitride ribbons. The TAO-DFT work proposes a nonempirical, spin-symmetry-restoration scheme that sets a system-dependent fictitious temperature for lowest singlet states of molecules. LeIFF represents valence electrons as dynamical spherical charge distributions in a compact force field for coupled nuclear and electronic dynamics at large scale. LetzElPhC is an open-source code that computes electron-phonon and exciton-phonon matrix elements from Quantum ESPRESSO DFPT output and interfaces with Yambo. The common thread is expanded physical scope, with fields, correlation, coupled dynamics and exciton-phonon coupling, at controlled computational cost.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
